# The build context is this whole directory (ops/consistency/) because the
# grading library compiles ops/consistency/grammar.yaml in — see Dockerfile.
# That makes it worth saying explicitly what must NOT ride along.
#
# `rust/target/` is the one that matters: it is gitignored, so a CI checkout
# never has it, but a local `docker build` would otherwise ship several GB of
# build artefacts as context before the first layer runs.
rust/target/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Not needed to build the binary. The corpus IS needed by `cargo test`, which
# runs in CI as its own job rather than inside the image build, so it is
# excluded here on purpose: the image carries the grammar it executes, not the
# tests that prove it executes it correctly.
testdata/
python/
collect/
schema/
stamp.py

# The committed generations are data the DEPLOYED meter reads from a mounted
# path (the ansible role places them), never something baked into the image —
# an image carrying one goatnet's intent would be a per-goatnet image.
intent/
